event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev_dispatch_1.md\", \"content\": \"Dispatch for dev — task d1 of campaign csrclaude.\\n\\nImplement, in the subject repo on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` (standard `unittest` module) with at least two test\\n   cases:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n3. Confirm `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 from the repo root\\n   before you reply. Paste the command's output in your reply.\\n\\nCommit your work to your own branch before replying (an empty branch under a\\nconfident reply is treated as work not done). In your reply, state plainly\\nwhether all three criteria above are met, and paste the test command's exact\\noutput.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

